  "prompt": "Pixel tycoon: a coaster-park management sim read from directly above. Quantized palette, no gradients and no hand tremor — every edge is a hard near-black outline (#1B1A2E) the way a Sobel pass leaves it. Emerald dithered lawns and ochre midway sand on dual-grid autotiles, bright cyan water with a single hard shoreline step, indigo night outside the fence. Saturated primary roofs — tomato, marigold, cyan. The isometric feeling is PAINTED, not projected (ADR-0019 clause 6): buildings carry a chunky brown side wall under a true-position roof, tree crowns are oversized with a rim light, and the camera preset in packages/shared/mapCamera.js turns the world a quarter-turn and tilts to the top of the permitted range. Per band (ADR-0019 clause 1, ADR-0021 clause 2): overview at 2.4 m/px drops every per-cell dither to flat blocks and flattens the buildings, because a 0.24-cell side wall is a quarter of a pixel there; mid is the base bake; close at 0.15 m/px thickens the dither, the side walls and the crowns, which is where the sim look actually lives. Axes (docs/goals/design-language-axes.md): A1 saturated quantized primaries, A2 hard value steps, A3 uniform near-black outline with zero displacement, A4 ordered dither over autotiles, B1 tiled ground, B2 stepped cyan water, B3 oversized round crowns, B4 side-walled blocks, B5 fat tube tracks, C2 primary badge discs"
}
